scn 1
# AR-11 mazeapproach: 4 movers walk a serpentine of 9 lanes (6 cells wide, 2-cell baffles, 4-cell gaps alternating
# ends, 112 cells long) to the nearest reachable spot of a goal sealed in a pocket under the last lane.
# `probe approach` reports when each unit reaches that spot and when its order completes. The walk takes
# about 8200 ticks (arrivals 7650-8700, one file; Retail's orders complete by 8360: the MV-14 free-path
# horizon), so it must NEVER be stopped mid-route:
# approach.dropped_unarrived_n stays 0 and every unit arrives before it completes. On the W2 head the
# approach grace (kTrappedRetire = 9000 from the order) outlasts the walk; W2 step 2 stamps the clock on
# ARRIVAL and drops the order there (kApproachRetire = 0), and this fixture guards that a long walk is
# not cut short by it.
name mazeapproach
ticks 10000
seed 7
map flat 144 122
probe approach
wall 16 16 112 2
wall 18 24 102 2
wall 24 32 102 2
wall 18 40 102 2
wall 24 48 102 2
wall 18 56 102 2
wall 24 64 102 2
wall 18 72 102 2
wall 24 80 102 2
wall 16 16 2 74
wall 126 16 2 74
wall 16 88 112 2
wall 16 90 112 2
wall 16 92 3 14
wall 125 92 3 14
wall 16 104 112 2
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
group A 0 m 4 cells 24,21 27,21 30,21 33,21
at 1 move A 72 98
